1 NOTE Easter of 1536 saw Manco Inca Yupanqui disgusted with Spanish Largess. The Spaniards were far from being "Liberators and Viracocha." They lusted after gold and enslaved his people. The Pizarro brother's insulted and mocked him at 
2 CONC every turn. The Spaniards invaded Peru right after a civil war had been fought between Atahualpa Yupanqui and his brother Huascar. The country and its people were in a turmpoil and factionated. The Spanish had just finished their 
2 CONC own war against the Moors and were well seasoned in the art of techniques of fighting. They had the latest technology in weaponry and horses.
2 CONT Manco fooled Hernando Pizarro and plied him with gold to keep in his good graces. So when he requested to go off to celebrate a festival he was allowed to do so. Manco Inca Yupanqui began a revolt that lasted for only a year and a
2 CONC  half. He was forced to retreat. He set up an independant Inca state at Vilacabamba. Governor Pizarro sought to win over Manco Inca with diplomacy. Manco responded by killing the governor's representatives. In response Pizarro had
2 CONC  Manco's sister wife, Cura Occlo, stripped, tied to a tree scourged with rods and then shot to death with arrows. Then Pizarro had her body floated down river in a basket into the Inca camp. Next he burned the high Priest, Villac 
2 CONC Umu burned alive and 15 other Inca captains who trusted Pizarro's promises. Manco made the mistake of taking in and giving refuge to some of Almago's renegade soldiers. One of them stabbed Manco in the back. Befire he died, he nam
2 CONC ed his son, Sayri Tupac as the new Inca ruler of Vilacabamba.
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Cobo Bernabe, History of the New World, Bk 12.
2 CONT Source 2.
