1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Newton Record; 27 Apr 1916, Thu; Page 3; Newton, Mississippi
2 CONT
2 CONT LAKE.
2 CONT From Forest Register
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. W. L. Pace returned Friday from Jackson, where she had spent some time with her daughter, Mrs. Tom Vance.
2 CONT *****
2 CONT There Newton Record; 27 Jul 1916, Thu; Page 4; Newton, Mississippi
2 CONT
2 CONT LAKE.
2 CONT (Items from Forest News. 21.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. W. L. Pace and daughter, Mary Lucy, are spending several days at Gum Springs.
2 CONT *****
2 CONT The Newton Record; 20 Dec 1928, Thu; Page 4; Newton, Mississippi
2 CONT
2 CONT W. L. Pace was re-elected as marshal last Tuesday. Mr. Pace has been known through this part of Mississippi as the best town marshal in the country. He has served many years and there never was a more fearless officer yet kind and
2 CONC  reasonable in all his dealings with the people whom he has to deal with.
2 CONT
2 CONT On account of Mr. Pace's good wife being very sick his two boys, Baker and Luther were called home last Sunday.
2 CONT *****
2 CONT The Newton Record; 27 Dec 1928, Thu; Page 3; Newton, Mississippi
2 CONT
2 CONT THANK YOU
2 CONT
2 CONT To our many friends who were so thoughtful of our loved one during her illness and so kind to us in our day of bereavement, we take this means of offering our thanks. We deeply appreciate your many words and acts of kindness and o
2 CONC f love. May the God of love, in whose presence she now abides forever, bless each of you and keep you.
