2 CONT It’s unclear the origins of the theory her maiden-name was Strayer.. But she should not be confused with:
2 CONT # Elizabeth Strayer (or Struyer) Guseman (b.08/05/1791–d.01/26/1864)   ([https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/KCSV-X9J KCSV-X9J]), 🪦[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/71688210/elizabeth-guseman 71688210], w/o John Guseman, d
2 CONC /o John S. Strayer & Anna Maria Swartz of WV & Fairfield Co. OH.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Strayer (1791–1864)  ([https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/KJ4J-4DB​​ KJ4J-4DB​​])
2 CONT # Elizabeth Strayer Winters (1808–1864) ([https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/L71W-QJ2 L71W-QJ2]) , 🪦[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/162595902/elizabeth-winter 162595902]
2 CONT These are not the same persons.  Nor should she be confused with Mrs. Elizabeth Smalls (c.1789–) widow of Yardley, Worcestershire, England, UK.
2 CONT
2 CONT >—FS, 03/10/2019, HalTeel, 
2 CONT >>''”I don’t believe her maiden name has been confirmed/verified?”''
