2 CONT 2em>> ❝ ANOTHER PIONEER GONE.  The funeral of Mrs. Sena Lanning, widow of the late Philip Lanning, pioneer merchant and postmaster at Gilmore, who died at her home in that town Monday morning of the infirmities of age, was held at
2 CONC  West Union cemetery Wednesday.  Mrs. Lanning was nearing 90 years. She is survived by her four children, Mrs. Nora Moore of New York City, Theodore Lanning, the well known Dennison merohant, John H. Lanning of Perry township and 
2 CONC D. P. Lanning, merchant and postmaster at Gilmore, succeeding the firm of P. Lanning & Sons, where his father's early business success was achieved. ❞
