2 CONT 2em>>..❝ [https://www.geni.com/people/Senia-Gardner-Lanning/6000000202121137911 '''Senia'''] got some money in lieu of land.  She married the future Gilmore merchant, [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-Lanning/6000000162398431821
2 CONC  Philip Lanning], a co-founder of that village. He and his son [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodore-Lanning/6000000202121422870 Theodore] have to be about the most affluent of our tribe. Precious indeed is my picture of [https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/Senia-Gardner-Lanning/6000000202121137911 '''Senia'''], portraying what the Gardners looked like before the onset of later in-law-ization… ❞
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Gardner/6000000033099708923 David Gardner] from Maryland 1788, d 1863, ┯ [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Gardner/6000000033099714039 Elizabeth] from Virginia 1791, d 1864 
2 CONT Nine children were born to them in Morgan Township, Greene County, Pennsylvania.  The family came to Perry Township, Tuscarawas County, Ohio in 1834.
