1 NOTE Illigitimate son of Francisca Gonzales Mateos and Capt. Gonzalo Pizarro Rodriguez de Avilar. Conqueror of Peru.
2 CONT Second Cousin of Hernan Cortes Pizzarro
2 CONT Conquered Peru 1532.
2 CONT Effectively and illegally exterminated the Inca dynasty of the Yupanqui by comitting regiscide.
2 CONT Made enemies with Almagro who was dissatisfied with the way the Inca riches were divided. He was given the southern part of the Inca empire which was mostly desert. After scattering the Inca Army under Manco he revolted against th
2 CONC e Pizarro family. Civil war broke out in Peru but was shortlived as Almagro was captured and suffered the same fate as Atahualpa.
2 CONT After returning to Spain Pizarro was assassinated in his chambers in Lima after he had attended Sunday mass by followers of Almagro. He fought bravely despite his age and ran through many of his assassins until he was stabbed in t
2 CONC he throat. As he fell he suffered many stabbings. His half brother, Martin de Alcantara also died fighting the assailants.
2 CONT ES.41091.AGI/1.16414.66.10//JUSTICIA,1074
