2 CONT
2 CONT The village of Bowerston was settled in the early 1800’s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two crude mills were built on the south side of
2 CONT
2 CONT Conotton Creek, which was then practically a
2 CONT
2 CONT wilderness. One mill was a sawmill, the other a
2 CONT
2 CONT gristmill. In 1804, Barnhard Bower and his brother John
2 CONT
2 CONT moved to the area and started to rebuild the mills. In
2 CONT
2 CONT 1816, the settlement called Bower's Mills was laid out.
2 CONT
2 CONT The village was first called Bowers Mill, then
2 CONT
2 CONT Bowersville, then Bowerstown, and finally Bowerston.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name was changed from Bowerstown to Bowerston
2 CONT
2 CONT because there was another town in Ohio by the name of
2 CONT
2 CONT Bowerstown. Bowerston was platted by David Bower,
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Hoover, and Nathaniel Bower on August 21, 1851
2 CONT
2 CONT and was filed in court August 2, 1852. Incorporation
2 CONT
2 CONT followed in 1881.
2 CONT
