2 CONT Will of Gabriel Swinehart 1798-1878 Will of Gabriel Swinehart Carroll County, Ohio In the name of the Benevolent Father of All, I Gabriel Swinehart of the County of Carroll and State of Ohio do make and publish this my last will a
2 CONC nd testament. Item 1 - I give and devise to my beloved wife in lieu of her dower the use of the farm on which we now reside during her natural lifetime together with all the personal property in belonging to me at the time of my d
2 CONC ecease - my said wife may sell at any time if necessary off said farm a sufficience to pay all my just debts. Item 2 - At the death of my wife the real estate aforesaid, I desire shall be sold together with all personal property r
2 CONC emaining on the farm or in any wise belonging to the estate and proceeds of same, distributed as follows, to wit. I give and devise of same to my daughter Lydia L. Swinehart the sum of seven hundred dollars and to my son Lesla Swi
2 CONC nehart one dollar and to my son Silas Swinehart one dollar and to each of the surviving heirs of my deceased daughter Ann McCluren one dollar and to Margaret Warner my daughter two hundred dollars and the balance of the remaining 
2 CONC estate to be equally divided among my three daughters Lydia L. Swinehart, Belinda Stonebrook, and Louisa Butterfield excepting said Belinda Stonebrook who shall receive two hundred dollars less that the third part of said remainin
2 CONC g estate said two hundred dollars to be divided equally between said Lydia L. Swinehart and Louisa Butterfield. I hereby nominate and appoint Homer Butterfield Executor of this my last will and testament. I do hereby revoke all fo
2 CONC rmer wills by me made in testimony hereof I have hereunto let my hand and seal this 21st day of October 1871. Gabriel Swinehart Signed and acknowledge in said Gabriel Swinehart in our presence and signed by us in his presence Eben
2 CONC ezer W. Laughlin W. G. Custer
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S., Sons of the American Revolution Membership Applications, 1889-1970 about Gabriel Swinehart Name:	Gabriel Swinehart SAR Membership:	86179 Birth Date:	20 Jul 1798 Death Date:	15 Jan 1878 Father:	 Adam Swinehart  Mother:	 Margr
2 CONC et Leslie  Spouse:	 Margret Fry  Children:	 Anne Swinehart 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabriel Swinehart Memorial Photos Flowers Edit Share Learn about removing the ads from this memorial... Birth: 	Jul. 20, 1798 Washington County Pennsylvania, USA Death: 	Jan. 15, 1878
2 CONT
2 CONT Sec. C Plot 111 Swinehart, Gabriel, b. 20 Jul 1798 Washington County, Pennsylvania, d. 15 Jan 1878, Sec C, Plot #111 cemetery transcript given by Larry Bower
2 CONT
2 CONT This cemetery was known as German Lutheran Church Cemetery in 1889. I am following the Messenger Family from Conn. to Ohio. I know they came with many families to settle Ohio. Some families even went farther west and some settled 
2 CONC in Penn. Marriage within these families was very common and I know for a fact the Swinehart Family is part of my mother's side. Unsure at this time but I remember this name in family stories. Gabriel Swinehart is buried beside Jam
2 CONC es and Elizabeth Messenger... Looking for more 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Margaret Frey Swinehart (1802 - 1883)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Longview Cemetery  Bowerston Harrison County Ohio, USA Plot: Sec C, Plot #111
2 CONT
