2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Dutton Bowers Memorial Photos Flowers Edit Share Learn about upgrading this memorial... Birth: 	Sep. 10, 1834 Death: 	Oct. 24, 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Nathaniel Bowers
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Nathaniel Bowers passed away at her home near Tiffin, Sunday afternoon at 3:20 o'clock, after an illness of slight duration.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a victim of congestion of the lungs, superinduced by grip.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will take place tomorrow afternoon, at 2 o'clock from the family residence. Rev. Mr. Fisher of the M.E. Church will conduct the services. the interment will be in the Tiffin Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are 5 daughter and 2 sons; Mesdames Peter Dipson, Atlantic; Millie Charbon, Tiffin; Emma L Colony, Sac County; and Mary E. Brown, Tiffin; and Ella Bowers, at home; Charles D, at home; and Joseph H, who lives near Tiffin;
2 CONC  Benjamine W Bowers and Joseph Bowers of Angora Neb. are step-sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Bowers was 75 years of age and had spend 45 years on the homestead, where the end came, having lived ever since she and her husband came from Ohio in 1864.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a woman of excellent character and warm heart and a large circle of pioneer friends will grieve deeply over her death.
2 CONT
