2 CONT Emma L Bowers Colony Memorial Photos Flowers Edit Share Learn about upgrading this memorial... Birth: 	Jul. 12, 1865 Johnson County Iowa, USA Death: 	Jun. 5, 1947
2 CONT
2 CONT EMMA COLONY, 82 DIES HERE Long Illness Takes Tiffin Resident; Services Wednesday Mrs. Emma L. Colony, 82, long-time resident of Tiffin, died Sunday afternoon at Mercy hospital after several months' illness. Funeral services will b
2 CONC e Wednesday at 2 p.m. at Oathout chapel with the Rev. Lloyd A. Tennant officiating. Burial will be in Tiffin cemetery. Mrs. Colony was born south of Tiffin, July 12, 1865, the daughter of Nathaniel and Rebecca Dutton Bowers. She w
2 CONC as married February 26, 1891 to Kyte Colony of Tiffin. With the exception of nine years which they spent near Sac City, the couple farmed near Tiffin their entire life. Survivors are three daughters, Mrs. Norval Matthes of North L
2 CONC iberty; Mrs. Oren Gray of Nampa, Idaho; Mrs. Clifford Reynolds of Tiffin; three sons, Arthur, Lynn and Virgil all of Tiffin; one sister, Mrs. Millie Carbon of Tiffin; one brother John Bowers of Coralville, and 16 grandchildren and
2 CONC  13 great grandchildren. A son John and her husband preceded her in death. 
2 CONT
