1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John August Christian Whitehair BIRTH	Mar 1760 Frederick County, Maryland, USA DEATH	1825 (aged 64–65) Aurora, Preston County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Old Saint Paul's Cemetery Aurora, Preston County, West Virgi
2 CONC niaChildren John Whitehair 1789–1889
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Whitehair 1798–1880
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/125161011/john-august_christian-whitehair
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN AUGUST CHRISTIAN3 WHITEHAIR (JOHN GEORGE (WEISHAAR)2, JOHANNES1 WEISHAAR) was born 1760 in Hagerstown, MD, and died 1825 in Aurora, Monongalia County, WV. He married EVA MARGARETTA TROY August 12, 1780 in Washington County, M
2 CONC D. She died in Aurora, WV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JOHN AUGUST CHRISTIAN WHITEHAIR: Weisshaar = Whitehair
2 CONT
2 CONT August Christian Whitehair, born about 1760, was the first of the family of the name in what is now Preston (then a part of Monongalia) County, VA (W VA). His sister Anna Maria Whitehair was also in the County and became the secon
2 CONC d wife of Thomas Reinhart. He came to Preston County from Maryland in 1788, and settled on the Jacob Elsey place. He had studied under the Oxford University graduate, Bartholomew Booth, at Booth's school, Delemere, near Hagerstown
2 CONC , MD. He was the first teacher in the Union District of the county and taught at Carmel in 1790. He is cited in the History of Preston County as an educational pioneer in Preston County and specifically within the German settlemen
2 CONC t. He attended the St Paul's Lutheran Church in Aurora. The minister of their church was the Reverend Jacob Weifer. Christian was married to Eva Margaretta Troy on 12 August 1780 in Washington County, MD. He was Constable of Monon
2 CONC galia County in 1806, 1808, and 1810. The dates of their deaths are unknown and they are assumed to be buried in the old St. Paul's Cemetery across the highway from the present church at Aurora.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT * Jonathon B. Whitehair (1798-1880)
2 CONT * George Whitehair (1783-1860)
