2 CONT 1em>>❝ [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-Lanning/6000000162398431821 '''PHILIP LANNING'''], merchant and Postmuster at Gilmore, was born in Washington Township, Tuscarawas Co., Ohio, in 1821. He is the second son of [https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/people/Joseph-Lanning/6000000162186119821 Joseph] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Phoebe-Lanning/6000000162397046849 Elizabeth Lanning], who emigrated to this county in 1818 [https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Lanning/6
2 CONC 000000162186119821  Joseph Lanning] was a native of New Jersey, and died in this county in 1878, at the ripe old age of eighty-one years.   His wife is still living and makes her home with her daughter, [https://www.geni.com/peopl
2 CONC e/Sarah-Denning/6000000162398436821 Sarah A.], wife of William Denning, of this township.     [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-Lanning/6000000162398431821 Philip Lanning] was raised in Tuscarawas County, and received only a lim
2 CONC ited education.  When about twenty-four years of age, he started out in life for himself.  In 1847, be was married to [https://www.geni.com/people/Senia-Gardner-Lanning/6000000202121137911 Senia Gardner], daughter of [https://www.
2 CONC geni.com/people/David-Gardner/6000000033099708923  David Garder], who came here from Pennsylvania in 1834. Our subject moved to Gilmore, his present place of business, in 1848, and entered the mercantile trade.  He first built a s
2 CONC mall store room, and lived in a part of the same for a number of years.  He hauled his goods from Wheeling, W Va., a distance of forty five miles. About this time he sold a horse and buggy, which furnished him money to start in bu
2 CONC siness. In 1861, he built a large store room, where he is now carrying on an immense mercantile trade.    The post office is located in his building. Four children have been born to him— [https://www.geni.com/people/Normanda-Rosa-
2 CONC Nora-Lanning-Moore/6000000202120821831 Nora Manda], wife of [https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Moore/6000000202120488858 S. G. Moore], of Galva, III.; [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodore-Lanning/6000000202121422870 Theodore], w
2 CONC ho was married in 1874. to Miss Nannie Mears, of Westchester, Ohio, and is now in partnership with his father; [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Lanning/6000000202121634825 John H.], who was married in 1878, to Miss Appie Billings
2 CONC ley, of Columbiana County; and [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Lanning/6000000202121584829 David P.], who is now living in Illinois.  Both our subject and wife are embers of the Methodist Protestant Church. Mr. Lanning is also 
2 CONC a member of the Masonic fraternity. His son, Theadore, is a member of the I. O. O. F.   He has been quite prosperous in business, although about two years ago their store and safe were burglarized, and there sustained a loss of 31
2 CONC ,000. They have also, from time to time, sus. tained heavy losses in different ways. He is now the owner of 130 acres of highly improved land, with new buildings on the same, besides a large nuount of village property, including a
2 CONC  heavy stock of goods. He is one of the first men of Washington Township. ❞
2 CONT
