2 CONT * grandson Earl’s 1895 S.F.Cal.-Gilmore O. Train travel Notes of him & his mother, Nora’s travel back to Gilmore, Ohio, to be with his dying grandfather, Philip Lanning : {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=600000022485097
2 CONC 2856&size=large}} [https://www.familysearch.org/photos/artifacts/208792377 ⓵﹙ ᶠʳᵒᵑᵗ ﹚] <span style="text-decoration: underline"> Trip from San Francisco to Dennison, Ohio, April 1895 </span>  <br> [https://www.geni.com/profile/ind
2 CONC ex/6000000202120821831 Ma] had received word from Gilmore that her father, [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-Lanning/6000000162398431821 '''Philip Lanning'''] was very ill. So about April 1/1895, [https://www.geni.com/profile/in
2 CONC dex/6000000202120821831 Ma] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Dr-Earl-Moore-Sr/6000000139240513845 myself] left San Francisco to go to Ohio.   We rode from Frisco via Sourhern Pacific to Ogden Utah. From Ogden via Union Pacific to 
2 CONC Denver + Rio Grande to Denver. We stayed in Denver about a day or so. [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Moore/6000000202122214873 Mrs. Hearon] met us and took us to a hotel near the railroad station. While here [https://www.geni.c
2 CONC om/profile/index/6000000202120821831 Ma] visited the Coles with whom we had lived with before leaving Denver for San Francisco. After leaving Denver we rode the Union Pacific to Kansas City. From there to St. Louis on the Missouri
2 CONC  Pacific. At St. Louis we changed cars  and continued the rest if our journey to Dennison Ohio. {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000224850973841&size=large}} [https://www.familysearch.org/photos/artifacts/208792957 
2 CONC ⓵﹙ ᵇᵃᶜᵏ ﹚]  via the Pennsylvania Railroad. We stayed only one day in Dennison, and then Uncle [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodore-Lanning/6000000202121422870 Theodore Lanning] drove us up to Gilmore.  My grandfather had been ver
2 CONC y sick but seemed to get better later on. [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000202120821831 Ma] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Dr-Earl-Moore-Sr/6000000139240513845 I] were in Gilmore until [https://www.geni.com/people/Phil
2 CONC ip-Lanning/6000000162398431821 '''Philip Lanning'''] died <span style="text-decoration: underline"> Aug. 17, 1895 </span>. <br> During the four months we were in Gilmore, [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000202120488858 Pa]
2 CONC , [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Moore/6000000202122214873 Johnnie], [https://www.geni.com/people/Mabel-Effie-Moore-Hearon/6000000202120703876 Birdie], + [https://www.geni.com/people/Roy-Moore/6000000202120989852 Roy] had come 
2 CONC to Brooklyn to live (101 Clark St.) and had started up another soap factory at 86 Broad St. New York City. <br> Our railroad trip from San Francisco was uneventful. Remember well the snow sheds over the Sierra Nevada Mountains and
2 CONC  the wonderful sunset we witnessed as we crossed over a section of the Great Salt Lake. 
2 CONT
