1 NOTE In 1559 El Inca Garcilasco de la Vega Yupanqui left his native Cuzco for Spain. he fought in the Mediterranian wars, took religious vows and wrote a stirring chronicle telling of the Inca Empire's rise and fall.  He was the first 
2 CONC great chronicler born in the New World. He, ( like myself in regard to being a descendand of Taino ancestors,) had to balance being a descendant of the Incas and of the Spanish
2 CONT conquistador. He eulogized both.
