0 @N6000000000537371223@ NOTE No creo que sea el padre, pero si el ascendiente
0 @N6000000003637320288@ NOTE Quechua Wayna Qhapaq "Juventud Espléndida"
1 CONT
1 CONT Huayna Capac (Quechua Wayna Qhapaq "splendid youth") was the eleventh Sapa Inca de the Inca Empire and sixth de the Hanan dynasty. He was the successor to Tupac Inca Yupanqui. His legitimate wife (and full-blooded galen rules sist
1 CONC er) was Coya Cusirimay. The pair produced no male heirs, but Huayna Capac produced as many as 50 or more children with other women, including Ninan Cuyochi, Huáscar, Atahualpa, Tupac Huallpa, Manco Inca Yupanqui, General Atoc, Paw
1 CONC llu Inca and Quispe Sisa - all de whom could be said to be his successors.
0 @N6000000000850681736@ NOTE Eugenia o Eufemia.
